{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1233674-changing-breeds-vargr","id":1233674,"title":"Changing breeds vargr","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-10T06:18:45-07:00","id":1233674,"title":"Changing breeds vargr","content":"So I have an idea for a different take on a werewolf but not Werewolf. But the problem is that in the changing breed it limits size. More or less I'm having troubles understanding how big can I get this wolf to be in feet with the right favors and aspects (not using giant merit) any help is great","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24308-vargrskol","name":"Vargrskol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T09:45:18-07:00","id":1233730,"title":"","content":"The system is made to be pretty modular, so you can add things in that allow you to reach greater heights. Some games flirt with really big Sizes, like Beast, even though they don't physically come into play.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest if there's a mechanic that allows for Size increases, but it doesn't go as high as you want, just change it until it fits your goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T19:46:27-07:00","id":1233890,"title":"","content":"Is this for use as an antagonist? If so then it is a Horror and you don't need to justify how it got its size, just give it the size rating you want it to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T14:23:00-07:00","id":1238693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1233674-changing-breeds-vargr?p=1233890#post1233890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this for use as an antagonist? If so then it is a Horror and you don't need to justify how it got its size, just give it the size rating you want it to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a character I'm creating for a short story/fanfiction but I want to remain as accurate to the cb book as possible, also with crossover characters from vtr and wtf maybe even a few others don't know yet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24308-vargrskol","name":"Vargrskol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T14:27:54-07:00","id":1238694,"title":"","content":"I was also wondering what size does a moose have being close to 7 feet at the shoulder and 800 to 1200 pounds ...thats about how big this character is in dire wolf form. Also if a werewolf in war form from wtf is size 7 and a vargr from cb is a size 7 in dire form which which would be taller ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24308-vargrskol","name":"Vargrskol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T16:11:27-07:00","id":1238712,"title":"","content":"A moose is Size 10, according to the book. A wolf in urshul would likely be shorter at the shoulder but comparable in width and broadness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T17:28:38-07:00","id":1238725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vargrskol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1233674-changing-breeds-vargr?p=1238694#post1238694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was also wondering what size does a moose have being close to 7 feet at the shoulder and 800 to 1200 pounds ...thats about how big this character is in dire wolf form. Also if a werewolf in war form from wtf is size 7 and a vargr from cb is a size 7 in dire form which which would be taller ?</div> </div> </div> </div>And just to clarify the dire form of the vargr in the cofd cb book is base size 5 but wth the size favor and extraordinary specimen aspect the size goes up by 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24308-vargrskol","name":"Vargrskol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T23:01:50-07:00","id":1238802,"title":"","content":"Well generally a werewolf in urshul form is Size 6, so it sounds like these guys are bigger in monster wolf form.<br /> <br /> From Werewolf's second edition, 'Urshul is a beast of legend. It looks the part of a wolf, but with the size of a horse. It\u2019s double the body mass of the Hishu form, and its shoulders stand at the same height her human shoulders do.'<br /> <br /> The Chronicles core does say Moose are Size 10, which I think is a bit of an overstatement, or at least averaging larger moose. Size doesn't just incorporate height, though, but is an abstract of weight and height and other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T00:39:38-07:00","id":1238816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1233674-changing-breeds-vargr?p=1238802#post1238802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well generally a werewolf in urshul form is Size 6, so it sounds like these guys are bigger in monster wolf form.<br /> <br /> From Werewolf's second edition, 'Urshul is a beast of legend. It looks the part of a wolf, but with the size of a horse. It\u2019s double the body mass of the Hishu form, and its shoulders stand at the same height her human shoulders do.'<br /> <br /> The Chronicles core does say Moose are Size 10, which I think is a bit of an overstatement, or at least averaging larger moose. Size doesn't just incorporate height, though, but is an abstract of weight and height and other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow ok thank you that helps a lot, and I agree about the moose size as well cause I've looked at other posts here and they says that a Clydesdale is size 8 and if you've ever looked at a picture of a moose and a Clydesdale they seem about the same in height weight and overall bulk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24308-vargrskol","name":"Vargrskol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T02:39:38-07:00","id":1238826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1233674-changing-breeds-vargr?p=1238802#post1238802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well generally a werewolf in urshul form is Size 6, so it sounds like these guys are bigger in monster wolf form.<br /> <br /> From Werewolf's second edition, 'Urshul is a beast of legend. It looks the part of a wolf, but with the size of a horse. It\u2019s double the body mass of the Hishu form, and its shoulders stand at the same height her human shoulders do.'<br /> <br /> The Chronicles core does say Moose are Size 10, which I think is a bit of an overstatement, or at least averaging larger moose. Size doesn't just incorporate height, though, but is an abstract of weight and height and other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a war form werewolf(wtf) ,bout how tall in feet would 1 stand? I know it's a size 7 and the book says something outrageous like 9 feet but what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24308-vargrskol","name":"Vargrskol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T06:47:52-07:00","id":1238893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vargrskol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1233674-changing-breeds-vargr?p=1238826#post1238826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a war form werewolf(wtf) ,bout how tall in feet would 1 stand? I know it's a size 7 and the book says something outrageous like 9 feet but what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>'Gauru is the classic wolfman of legend. Enormous, fearsome, and devastating, Gauru Uratha weigh almost four times their Hishu counterparts. While bipedal, they stand one and a half times their Hishu height. They\u2019re bulky, with arms the size of most people\u2019s waists, legs like tree trunks, and teeth like chef\u2019s knives.'<br /> <br /> 1 and a half times their Hishu height means they would be 9 feet once their human form was 6. You can get even larger with the Giant Merit, or smaller with Small-Framed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T22:38:34-07:00","id":1240332,"title":"","content":"How many mage spells/spirit numina/ werewolf gifts can a changing breed learn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24308-vargrskol","name":"Vargrskol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T08:35:46-07:00","id":1251674,"title":"","content":"Also when a werewolf travels to the shadow ,does the distance he covers equal the same distance one would cover if they traveled in the material world?<br /> <br /> And how long can a changing breed stay in their hybrid/ primal form ?(not war form)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24308-vargrskol","name":"Vargrskol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-05T09:10:44-07:00","id":1251682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vargrskol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1233674-changing-breeds-vargr?p=1251674#post1251674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also when a werewolf travels to the shadow ,does the distance he covers equal the same distance one would cover if they traveled in the material world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, the hisil is based off of memories and perception, not just of humans. So a place that may seem bigger than it actually is in the real world may actually be bigger in the hisil. And like in the West how we don't have a 13th floor in many buildings, or in some areas near China a 4th or Canada, apparently, a 13th Highway, these places often likely exist in the hisil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-05-2018, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T09:00:26-07:00","id":1252229,"title":"","content":"Thank you and just to sum up what my character might look like in primal/dire form there is a gift in wtf called Primal Form a favored form of the pure roughly 7 feet tall at the shoulder, around 9 feet tall with the head raised about 12 feet long from nose to tail and close to 400 to 500 lbs .my character is slightly smaller than that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24308-vargrskol","name":"Vargrskol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}